27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #No, these are not development modules—they are the actual low-level hardware drivers required for
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #your Intensity Pro 4K to function.
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #In this context, DKMS stands for Dynamic Kernel Module Support.
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Because Blackmagic's drivers are proprietary and not built directly into the official Linux kernel
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #source tree, DKMS compiles the driver modules (`blackmagic` and `blackmagic-io`) specifically for
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #your running kernel (`7.2.2-arch1-1`). This mechanism also ensures that whenever your kernel
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #updates in the future, the system will automatically recompile these hardware drivers so the card
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #continues to work.
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27865c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Now that the kernel drivers are built and installed, you can proceed with starting the background
