278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.003 18.09KB 3.56s
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #The official Arch Linux `ffmpeg` binary is built without `--enable-decklink` (due to license
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #incompatibilities between FFmpeg's GPL and Blackmagic's SDK). Because of that, the command exited
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #without querying the device.
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #To verify the card via command line without compiling a custom FFmpeg, you have two reliable
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #options:
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Check the device nodes
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Run:
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
278672a5 [gemini-3.8-flash] #ls -l /dev/blackmagic*
278672a6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
278672a6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
278672a6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #If the kernel drivers attached to the card correctly, you will see a character device such as
278672a6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`/dev/blackmagic/io0`.
278672a6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
278672a6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Check the kernel initialization logs
