2786886f [gemini-3.8-flash] #It is related, but with an important distinction:
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`DeckLinkAPIDispatch.cpp` is a C++ source file, not a header (`.h`) file.
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Standard compiler include paths (such as `-I/usr/include`) tell the compiler where to find
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`#include` headers during compilation. However, `make` is trying to compile
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`DeckLinkAPIDispatch.cpp` itself directly into an object file, and it is looking for that file at
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #the hardcoded prerequisite path:
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #../../include/DeckLinkAPIDispatch.cpp
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Because that relative directory does not exist relative to where you cloned `bmdtools`, `make`
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #aborts before the compiler is even invoked.
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #To resolve this, the Makefile needs the directory variable `SDK_PATH` defined so it can locate the
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`.cpp` source file. You can check where that file lives on your system with:
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #find /usr -name "DeckLinkAPIDispatch.cpp" 2>/dev/null
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Once located, passing `SDK_PATH=<directory>` will tell `make` where both the headers and that
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #source file reside.
27868870 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
