279e4b8d [skid@archlinux] can you see in history the results of tool calls?
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.048 199.5KB 6.98s
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #In this current conversation, no tools have been invoked yet, so there are no tool call results in
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #our session context.
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #If you mean within `relay.ts` itself: yes.
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #When a model invokes a function, `relay.ts` processes the call and stores the result in
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`rohaHistory`:
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. `processToolCalls()` executes the requested function (such as `read_time`, `submit_file`,
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`fetch_file`, or `tag_slop`).
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. An entry with `role: "tool"`, `tool_call_id`, `name`, and the returned `content` is pushed into
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`rohaHistory`.
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. In subsequent turns (and in recursive turns within `relay()`), those entries are serialized and
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #returned to the model:
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   - For Google / Gemini: formatted as `role: "function"` with a `functionResponse` part.
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   - For OpenAI / DeepSeek: formatted as standard `role: "tool"` messages linked to `tool_call_id`.
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   - For Anthropic: mapped to corresponding tool result blocks.
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #As long as history is not reset (`/reset`) or stripped, the model retains full visibility into
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #previous tool results.
279e4c04 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
