279efd8f [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.009 32.79KB 4.53s
279efd8f [gemini-3.8-flash] #Yes. In Godot, `ClassDB` is both the engine's internal reflection database and an exposed
279efd8f [gemini-3.8-flash] #singleton within that very database.
279efd8f [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279efd8f [gemini-3.8-flash] #Key aspects of how this works:
279efd8f [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. The Role of `ClassDB`:
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   It is the central repository where Godot registers all `Object`-derived classes, along with
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #their methods, properties, signals, constants, and inheritance hierarchies. Tools that dump the
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Godot API (such as `--dump-extension-api` for GDExtension) query `ClassDB` directly to produce
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #these lists.
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Self-Reference:
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   Because `ClassDB` is itself an engine class derived from `Object`, it gets registered into the
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #class hierarchy alongside every other class. This is why `ClassDB` appears inside the `"object"`
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #list in your file.
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Separation from Variants:
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #   Notice that the `"variant"` types (such as `Vector3`, `Transform3D`, `Color`, `Array`) are
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #listed separately from `"node"`, `"resource"`, and `"object"`. This aligns with Godot's internal
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #architecture: primitive engine types are handled by the `Variant` system rather than registered as
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #`Object` classes inside `ClassDB`.
279efd90 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
