279f3cfc [gemini-3.8-flash] #A few observations regarding how Godot handles class hierarchies and data querying in this script:
279f3cfc [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3cfc [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Self-inheritance with `ClassDB.is_parent_class`: In Godot, `ClassDB.is_parent_class(a,
279f3cfc [gemini-3.8-flash] #b)` returns `false` when `a == b`. As a result, the base classes `"Node"`, `"Resource"`, and
279f3cfc [gemini-3.8-flash] #`"Object"` themselves might be omitted from their respective arrays unless explicitly checked or
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #included.
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Overlapping categories: Because all engine classes inherit from `Object`, the `objects`
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #array will contain nodes, resources, and editor types. If the goal is a mutually exclusive
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #classification (for instance, general objects that are neither nodes nor resources), an exclusion
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #check may be needed.
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Editor classes coverage: Checking prefixes (`Editor` and `ResourceImporter`) captures the
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #primary editor types, but certain editor-specific classes in tools builds (such as `FileSystemDock`
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #or `ScriptEditor`) use different naming conventions. If comprehensive coverage of editor types is
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #required, checking against `EditorInterface` or editor modules may be beneficial.
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Version status: `Engine.get_version_info()` provides `major`, `minor`, and `patch`, but
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #also includes a `"status"` key (such as `"stable"` or `"dev"`). If version matching needs to
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #distinguish preview builds from releases, that field can be helpful.
279f3cfd [gemini-3.8-flash] #
