279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° (undefined+NaN[2275]) 7.012KB 3.08s
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Yes, you can extract descriptions, though the mechanism depends on where the script is executed.
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. In an Editor Context (EditorPlugin / EditorScript)
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #In tools/editor builds, `EditorHelp` (an internal editor class) handles documentation, but it is
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #not directly exposed to standard GDScript.
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #However, Godot ships with the full XML documentation bundled inside editor builds. The editor
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #parses these XML resources into an internal cache. If running as an `EditorScript`, documentation
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #for classes, methods, properties, and signals is available through the `EditorInterface` and
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #translation/doc utilities, though direct GDScript bindings for raw docstrings from `ClassDB` are
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #intentionally omitted in release builds to keep binary sizes compact.
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Extracting from the Engine's Extension API / Dump
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #If this script is run via the command line (headless/standalone), the canonical way to obtain the
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #complete documentation dictionary—matching the online manual word-for-word—is via the engine's
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #built-in API dump command:
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #godot --dump-extension-api
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #This generates an `extension_api.json` file containing the full AST of the engine, including:
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Class briefs and descriptions.
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Method arguments, return types, and descriptions.
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #• Properties, signals, constants, and theme items with their documentation comments.
279f3eb9 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #You can then parse this JSON within your script using `FileAccess` and `JSON.parse_string()` to
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #extract and map descriptions directly to your schema entries.
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Parsing Doc XMLs Directly
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #Godot's documentation is maintained as XML files in the engine repository (`doc/classes/*.xml`). If
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #your tool runs in an environment with access to Godot's source or cloned docs, an `XMLParser` can
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #be used to read the `<brief_description>` and `<description>` tags for each class.
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #Would you like to see an implementation using the `extension_api.json` dump or an `XMLParser`
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #approach?
279f3eba [gemini-3.8-flash] #
