2848ae5a [deepseek-flash] #comparisons, not calls. Only calls get hoisted into helpers.
2848ae5a [deepseek-flash] #- `mark_input_handled` reads a bit oddly as a one-liner, but it keeps the call chain out of
2848ae5a [deepseek-flash] #`_unhandled_input` and gives you one place to change if you ever swap the viewport/tree.
2848ae5a [deepseek-flash] #- If you'd rather not have a function that just wraps two lines, the alternative is a single local:
2848ae5a [deepseek-flash] #`var viewport := get_viewport()` then `viewport.set_input_as_handled()`. Same effect, no extra
2848ae5a [deepseek-flash] #function. Your call which you prefer.
