284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #A few observations:
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #• scrape.gd*
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #- This is a headless schema exporter. Run it with `--headless --script scrape.gd` and it dumps the
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #class list to JSON, then exits.
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #- It extends `SceneTree`, which is the standard way to write a command-line Godot tool that doesn't
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #need a main scene.
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Category overlap is present: every `Node` and `Resource` also inherits `Object`, so those classes
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #will appear in both the `node`/`resource` arrays and the `object` array. If you want mutually
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #exclusive categories, classify by the most specific ancestor first.
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Writing to `res://godot_api_schema.json` works from the project directory in editor/development
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #builds, but `res://` is read-only in exported projects. For a portable tool, accept an output path
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #argument or write to `user://` / the executable's base directory.
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `is_editor_class` includes `ResourceImporter`, which doesn't begin with `Editor` but is correctly
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #grouped as editor-related.
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `TYPE_MAX` and `type_string` are Godot 4 `Variant.Type` API.
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #• classdb.txt*
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #- This matches the Godot 4 `ClassDB` documentation. One formatting note: the method list has return
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #types and names concatenated (e.g., `boolcan_instantiate`), so it isn't directly parseable as-is.
284abfda [kimi-k2.7-code] #
284abfdb [kimi-k2.7-code] #If you want, I can suggest changes to make the categories disjoint or make the output path
