28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.007 19.73KB 3.81s
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Because `/dev/sda` is a mechanical spinning hard drive (HDD), random read/write seek latency is the
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #biggest bottleneck when transferring thousands of small files. Standard recursive tools tend to
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #jump back and forth across sectors.
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #The fastest way to write to a spinning disk is a streaming `tar` pipeline. Reading from the
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #NVMe happens in memory, and writing to the HDD happens sequentially in large blocks, minimizing
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #head movement.
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #The Fastest Command (Sequential Pipeline)
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #sudo tar -C /srv/http/grid -cf - . | sudo tar -C /mnt/grid26 -xf -
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #With a Progress Bar (if `pv` is installed)
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #If you have `pv` installed (`sudo pacman -S pv`), you can see the throughput and volume
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #transferred:
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #sudo tar -C /srv/http/grid -cf - . | pv | sudo tar -C /mnt/grid26 -xf -
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #Why this is faster for spinning disks:
28b380f6 [gemini-3.8-flash] #1. Zero head thrashing: It avoids `rsync`'s two-way checking and directory traversing
28b380f7 [gemini-3.8-flash] #overhead.
28b380f7 [gemini-3.8-flash] #2. Preserves everything: Exact ownership (`http:http`), permissions, modes, and symlinks
28b380f7 [gemini-3.8-flash] #remain intact.
28b380f7 [gemini-3.8-flash] #3. Sequential write stream: The Linux page cache and HDD write buffer can write data to
28b380f7 [gemini-3.8-flash] #disk in continuous track sectors rather than random small sector writes.
28b380f7 [gemini-3.8-flash] #
