28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 kimi-k2.7-code 🜁 🪠 🧊 $0.070 258.5KB 60.49s
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #Thanks for sharing these. The project appears to be a native Linux embedded host/service layer for
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #a DSP/remote-control stack (`dsptool`), mixing system interfaces, networking, media I/O, and an
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #HTTP RPC front end.
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #A few high-level observations:
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #• Architecture*
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- The codebase is mostly header-only and compiled into a small number of `.cpp` entry points
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #(`fit3.cpp`, `displaytest.cpp`, `nativetool.cpp`, `opensocket.cpp`). That keeps builds simple but
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #gives each translation unit a very large include surface.
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- A central `Stereo` singleton in `headless.h` owns Redis/Valkey, process management, and event
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #routing, while `fit3.cpp` sets up the HTTP and signal handling. Several subsystems still carry
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #older names (`Stereo`, `nitrohost`, `bios`) alongside newer ones (`fit3`).
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #• Notable subsystem notes*
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `alsaaudio.h` — wraps card enumeration and simple PCM playback/capture tests. There is a
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #hard-coded test that opens `"default"` and writes generated square-wave audio.
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `drmdisplay.h` / `eglgraphics.h` — KMS/GBM/EGL init path for headless GLES output. Some teardown
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #paths are commented out and the flip path still does a full `drmModeSetCrtc` each frame rather than
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #true atomic/page-flip double buffering.
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `headless.h` — contains a `Process` class that forks child apps and pipes stdio. It also hosts
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #the JSON-RPC dispatcher (`InvokeRPC`). The dispatcher is a long `if/else` chain that could be
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #table-driven if it keeps growing.
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `http.h` — small threaded HTTP server with POST-based RPC and static file serving. It has
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #path-sanitization checks (`..`) and a keep-alive path, and it sets a 3-second receive timeout per
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #connection.
28ba8ba9 [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `redis.h` — synchronous hiredis wrapper plus async `Scribe`/`Sink` helpers. The async paths start
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #threads that are never joined.
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `json.h` — custom JSON parser. It distinguishes `Integer` from `Number` and uses `wchar_t` /
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #`codecvt_utf8` internally.
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `crypto.h` — provides SHA-512 via OpenSSL EVP (and labels it `sha3_512` in the EVP path) or
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #Common Crypto on macOS.
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #• Things worth tightening if you plan to extend this*
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Many places use raw `new` and never `delete` (e.g., `Process`, `HttpConnection`, `JSValue`
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #subtrees in the RPC dispatcher). For a long-running daemon that matters.
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Several functions ignore return values or partially handle errors (common in bring-up code, but
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #easy to harden).
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Globals/statics such as `fd`, `buffers`, `frame_data` in `video.h` make that module
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #non-reentrant.
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `headless.h` line `utf8 src="stereo.h " Stringify(__line__);` is almost certainly not what was
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #intended; `Stringify(__line__)` expands to `"__line__"`, not the current line number. Use
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #`std::to_string(__LINE__)` instead.
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `crypto.h` EVP path calls `EVP_sha3_512()` while the function name says SHA-512. If you want
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #SHA-512, use `EVP_sha512()`; if you want SHA3-512, rename the function to avoid confusion.
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `base64.h` decode routine does not validate padding or reject non-alphabet characters, and the
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #encode/decode alphabets differ (`+` vs `,`), which is intentional per the comment but easy to trip
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #over.
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #If you want, I can look deeper at any specific area — for example, converting the RPC dispatcher to
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #a registration table, hardening the Redis lifecycle, or finishing the DRM atomic/page-flip path.
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #Just let me know which files or problems are current.
28ba8baa [kimi-k2.7-code] #
