28ba98fa [kimi-k2.7-code] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 kimi-k2.7-code 🜁 🪠 🧊 $0.099 348.0KB 43.72s
28ba98fa [kimi-k2.7-code] #I’ve reviewed the shared files. A few observations on the dsptool stack:
28ba98fa [kimi-k2.7-code] #
28ba98fa [kimi-k2.7-code] #• Architecture*
28ba98fa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Native C++ backend (`fit3.cpp` entry point) with an HTTP server, JSON-RPC dispatch, Redis/Valkey
28ba98fa [kimi-k2.7-code] #integration, and a web frontend served from `web/`.
28ba98fa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Header-heavy implementation: most logic lives in `.h` files included directly.
28ba98fa [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Cross-platform scaffolding with `#ifdef __APPLE__`, `__linux__`, `_WIN32` guards.
28ba98fa [kimi-k2.7-code] #
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #• Notable subsystems*
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Audio: ALSA capture/playback and a software synth (`synth.h`).
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Graphics: DRM/KMS + GBM + EGL path (`drmdisplay.h`), plus a framebuffer snapshot path.
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Networking: HTTP/IPv4/IPv6 server, Redis/Valkey client, socket wrappers.
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Hardware interfaces: serial/udev, V4L2 video, Bluetooth SDP, NMEA 2000, CEC.
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #• Code-quality notes*
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Several macros invoke `raise(SIGSTOP)` on error (e.g., `FDErrorCheck`, `ErrorCheck`). That may be
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #intentional for debugging, but it will halt a production server.
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #- There is a lot of global/static state (`stereo`, `HttpSocket4/6`, `infoCache`, etc.).
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `alloca` is used in several ALSA/DRM paths.
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #- `Process::start` uses `vfork` + `execvp` without post-`_exit` error handling.
28ba98fb [kimi-k2.7-code] #- Some files are stubs or nearly empty (`ramis.h`, the `snapshotFB` override in `fit3.cpp`).
