28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.005 547B 6.17s
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #To reset permissions recursively on a folder in Arch Linux, you can use `chmod` and optionally
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #`chown`.
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Reset permissions to standard defaults (755 for directories, 644 for files):*
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #find "/path/to/plain data" -type d -exec chmod 755 {} \;
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #find "/path/to/plain data" -type f -exec chmod 644 {} \;
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Or, if you just want a uniform permission (e.g. 755) on everything:*
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #chmod -R 755 "/path/to/plain data"
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #• If you also want to reset ownership to yourself:*
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #sudo chown -R $USER:$USER "/path/to/plain data"
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Notes:*
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b70 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Quote the path since it contains a space (`plain data`).
28bc2b71 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `755` = owner can read/write/execute, others can read/execute — typical for directories.
28bc2b71 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `644` = owner can read/write, others can read only — typical for files.
28bc2b71 [claude-sonnet-5] #- If you want directories executable (so they can be entered) but files not executable, use the two
28bc2b71 [claude-sonnet-5] #separate `find` commands above rather than a single `chmod -R`.
28bc2b71 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bc2b71 [claude-sonnet-5] #Let me know your actual folder path and desired permission scheme (e.g. private vs shared) if you
28bc2b71 [claude-sonnet-5] #want a more tailored command.
28bc2b71 [claude-sonnet-5] #
