28bcaeb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #	add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable";
28bcaeb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #	root /mnt/grid26;
28bcaeb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #	gzip_static on;
28bcaeb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #	gunzip on;
28bcaeb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #}
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #Check the module is available first:
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #nginx -V 2>&1 | grep -o http_gunzip_module
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #This way you don't need to rely on BunnyCDN's origin request headers being correct — it'll work no
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #matter what.
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #• If you still want to configure BunnyCDN's side:*
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #In the Bunny dashboard, under your Pull Zone settings, look in:
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Caching tab — there may be an option related to forwarding headers or compression
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #handling.
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Origin settings — sometimes labeled something like "Forward Accept-Encoding" or "Origin
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #compression".
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #I'm not fully confident on the exact current label/location since Bunny's dashboard UI changes
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #fairly often — I'd suggest searching their docs for `Accept-Encoding` or `gzip` specifically to get
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #the precise current setting name, rather than me guessing and sending you to the wrong tab.
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #• My suggestion:* apply `gunzip on;` on your nginx config now (quick, guaranteed fix), and
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #treat the BunnyCDN setting as optional/secondary — it removes a dependency on CDN behavior that
28bcaeb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #might change or vary per request type.
