28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #Understanding the "Tainted Canvas" WebGL Error
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #(Side note: your message had a stray `[200~` at the start — that's a leftover bracketed-paste
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #terminal artifact, not an actual error code. No need to worry about it.)
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #What This Error Means
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #Uncaught SecurityError: Failed to execute 'texImage2D' on 'WebGL2RenderingContext':
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #Tainted canvases may not be loaded.
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #This happens when you try to load an image, video, or another canvas into a WebGL texture,
28cafdb8 [claude-sonnet-5] #but the browser has marked that source as "tainted" due to cross-origin restrictions.
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #A canvas/image becomes "tainted" when it contains pixel data loaded from a different origin
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #without proper CORS permission. Once tainted, the browser blocks WebGL from reading its
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #pixel data — this is a security measure to prevent silently stealing image data from other sites.
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #Common Causes
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #1. Loading an image from a CDN (like BunnyCDN) that doesn't send CORS headers
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #2. Missing `crossOrigin` attribute on the `<img>` element
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #3. Drawing a cross-origin image onto a 2D `<canvas>` first, then trying to use that canvas as a
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #WebGL texture
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #4. Loading local files via `file://` protocol
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #How to Fix It
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #1. Set `crossOrigin` on the Image Before Loading
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #function loadImageForTexture(url, onLoad) {
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #	const image = new Image();
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #	image.crossOrigin = "anonymous";
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #	image.onload = () => onLoad(image);
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #	image.src = url;
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #}
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Important: `crossOrigin` must be set before* `src` is assigned.
28cafdb9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #2. Ensure the Server Sends CORS Headers
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #The image server (BunnyCDN in your case) needs to respond with:
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #• On BunnyCDN*, you can enable this in your Pull Zone settings:
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #- Go to your Pull Zone → Headers
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #- Add a custom header:
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #Or restrict it to your specific domain instead of `*` if you want tighter security:
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://yourdomain.com
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #3. Double-Check Both Sides Match
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #CORS requires both:
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #- ✅ `crossOrigin` set on the client-side `Image` object
28cafdba [claude-sonnet-5] #- ✅ `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header from the server
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #If either is missing, the canvas becomes tainted.
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #Quick Debugging Checklist
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #╭─────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────╮
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Check                                  │  Status    │
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #├─────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────┤
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #│  image.crossOrigin = "anonymous" set?   │  ?         │
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Server sends Access-Control-Allow-*?   │  ?         │
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Are you loading from BunnyCDN domain?  │  ?         │
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Same headers present on redirect URLs? │  ?         │
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #╰─────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────╯
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #
28cafdbb [claude-sonnet-5] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
