28dc628e [claude-sonnet-5] #KDE Menu Editor "Delete" — What It Actually Does
28dc628e [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc628e [claude-sonnet-5] #• Short answer: No, it won't uninstall the package.*
28dc628e [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc628e [claude-sonnet-5] #What Menu Editor's Delete Actually Does
28dc628e [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #KDE's Menu Editor (`kmenuedit`) only manages `.desktop` files — the shortcuts/entries that
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #make apps appear in your application launcher. Clicking Delete there:
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #- ✅ Removes the app's icon/entry from your Kickoff/Application menu
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #- ❌ Does NOT remove the actual Falkon binary
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #- ❌ Does NOT free up disk space
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #- ❌ Does NOT remove dependencies
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #The program will still be fully installed and runnable from a terminal (`falkon`) or via `krunner`
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #(Alt+Space) even after deleting it from the menu.
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #Why This Distinction Matters
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #╭─────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────┬──────────────────────╮
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Action                     │  Removes from Menu   │  Uninstalls Package  │
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #├─────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #│  `kmenuedit` → Delete       │  ✅ Yes               │  ❌ No                │
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #│  `sudo pacman -Rns falkon`  │  ✅ Yes (indirectly)  │  ✅ Yes               │
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #╰─────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────┴──────────────────────╯
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #Pacman removal will also clean up the menu entry automatically, since the `.desktop` file
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #is part of the package.
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #Recommendation
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #If your goal is to actually uninstall Falkon (not just hide it), stick with:
28dc628f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc6290 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc6290 [claude-sonnet-5] #sudo pacman -Rns falkon
28dc6290 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc6290 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc6290 [claude-sonnet-5] #Only use Menu Editor's Delete if you want to keep the program installed but just hide it from the
28dc6290 [claude-sonnet-5] #app launcher (e.g., you use it occasionally via terminal but don't want menu clutter).
28dc6290 [claude-sonnet-5] #
