28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.020 17.73KB 9.42s
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #Recap: Should Home Users Bother Uninstalling Falkon?
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #Good question. Here's the honest breakdown:
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #Most Home Users: Probably Not Worth It
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #Falkon is a lightweight browser (QtWebEngine-based) — it's small, uses minimal disk space,
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #and doesn't run any background services when you're not using it. For most people, leaving it
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #installed but unused causes zero practical harm:
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #- No background processes eating RAM
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #- No noticeable disk space impact (a few MB)
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Won't slow down boot time or menu loading
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #When It Does Make Sense to Remove
28dc7146 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #╭─────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────╮
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Situation                              │  Worth Removing?    │
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #├─────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Just want a cleaner app menu           │  Use kmenuedit hide │
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Minimal/embedded system, low storage   │  Yes                │
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Security concern (unused browser)      │  Yes                │
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  "I'll never use it, why is it here"    │  Optional/cosmetic  │
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #│  It's part of kde-network-meta bundle   │  Usually leave it   │
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #╰─────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────╯
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #Better Option for Most People: Just Hide It
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #If your actual goal is just "I don't want to see it in my menu" rather than reclaiming disk
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #space, the simpler and safer path is:
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #kmenuedit → select Falkon → Delete
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #This keeps the package installed (so no dependency conflicts with `kde-network-meta`), but removes
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #the icon clutter from your launcher — which is probably the actual annoyance, not disk usage.
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #Bottom Line
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #Unless you're short on storage or have a specific reason (security policy, minimal install, etc.),
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #it's not really necessary to fight the dependency chain just to remove an unused ~10MB
28dc7147 [claude-sonnet-5] #browser. Hiding it from the menu solves the everyday annoyance with zero risk.
28dc7148 [claude-sonnet-5] #
