28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #Yes — That's Exactly What Happened, and It's a Fair Complaint
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #How This Occurs
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #Metapackages like `kde-network-meta` are dependency bundles. When you (or an
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #installer/installation script) installed something like `plasma-meta` or a KDE group package, it
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #silently pulled in a whole tree of "recommended" apps — Falkon included — without asking you
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #individually about each one.
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #This is a real, well-known criticism of meta-package-driven installs: you get convenience
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #at the cost of implicit consent. You didn't choose Falkon. A packaging decision chose it
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #for you.
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #Why This Happens on Arch (and Similar Distros)
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #╭──────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────╮
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Install Method               │  Consent Level                    │
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #├──────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #│  sudo pacman -S falkon        │  Explicit — you chose it           │
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #│  sudo pacman -S plasma-meta   │  Implicit — bundled dependency     │
28dc7f0f [claude-sonnet-5] #│  Distro's default ISO/install │  Zero — decided before you existed │
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #╰──────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────╯
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #Arch is supposed to be minimal and user-controlled compared to Ubuntu/Fedora, but KDE's own
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #meta-packages still carry this "batteries included" philosophy from upstream KDE, not from Arch
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #itself.
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #How to Prevent This Going Forward
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #1. Inspect Before Installing Meta-packages
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #pacman -Si kde-network-meta
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #Look at the Depends On field before you install a metapackage — you'll see the full list
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #before it lands on your system.
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #2. Use `--asdeps` Awareness
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #Check whether something was pulled in as a dependency vs. explicitly requested:
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #pacman -Qi falkon | grep "Install Reason"
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #If it says `Installed as a dependency`, that confirms it was never something you asked for
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #directly.
28dc7f10 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #3. Avoid Broad Meta-packages Going Forward
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #Instead of:
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #sudo pacman -S plasma-meta
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #Consider a more surgical install:
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #sudo pacman -S plasma-desktop konsole dolphin
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #You lose some convenience, but you gain explicit control over exactly what touches your
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #system — which sounds like exactly what you want.
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #Bottom Line
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #You're not wrong to be annoyed. "It came bundled" is a legitimate root cause, not user error. The
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #fix isn't just removing Falkon once — it's changing how you install KDE components going
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #forward so this doesn't keep happening silently.
28dc7f11 [claude-sonnet-5] #
