28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #Default Application Resolution in Arch Linux
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #When an app like Discord opens an image, the resolution generally follows this chain:
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #1. MIME Type Associations (XDG)
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #Most desktop apps use the XDG MIME Applications specification. The lookup order is
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #typically:
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `~/.config/mimeapps.list` (user overrides)
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `/etc/xdg/mimeapps.list` (system-wide overrides)
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `~/.local/share/applications/mimeapps.list`
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `/usr/share/applications/mimeapps.list` (defaults set by packages)
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #These files map MIME types (e.g., `image/png`) to `.desktop` file names.
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #2. The `.desktop` Files
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #Once a MIME type is matched to an application ID, the system looks in:
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c89 [claude-sonnet-5] #- `~/.local/share/applications/`
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #- `/usr/share/applications/`
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #- `/usr/local/share/applications/`
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #for a matching `.desktop` file, which contains the actual `Exec=` line telling the system what
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #binary to run.
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #3. Tools That Do the Lookup
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #Discord (an Electron app) typically shells out to `xdg-open`, which:
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #1. Checks `mimeapps.list` for the MIME type
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #2. Falls back to querying `xdg-mime query default <mimetype>`
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #3. Executes the resolved `.desktop` entry
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #Checking/Changing It Yourself
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #You can inspect and modify these associations with:
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] ## Check current default for image/png
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #xdg-mime query default image/png
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] ## Set a new default
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #xdg-mime default org.gnome.gimp.desktop image/png
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8a [claude-sonnet-5] #Or manually edit `~/.config/mimeapps.list`:
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #[Default Applications]
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #image/png=feh.desktop
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #image/jpeg=feh.desktop
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #Desktop Environment Overrides
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #If you're running GNOME, KDE, or another DE, their Settings → Default Applications panel
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #usually just writes to the same `mimeapps.list` file, so changes there and via `xdg-mime` are
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #interchangeable.
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #If Discord is opening something unexpected, checking `~/.config/mimeapps.list` first is usually the
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #fastest way to diagnose it.
28dc8c8b [claude-sonnet-5] #
