28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #That makes sense actually — it's likely not an image MIME type issue at all. Here's why:
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #The Likely Cause: URL vs File
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #Discord images are usually hosted on their CDN (`cdn.discordapp.com` or `media.discordapp.net`).
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #When you click an image in Discord, it often doesn't download it locally first — instead it just
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #opens the URL in your default browser.
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #That means the relevant setting isn't `image/png`, it's the URL scheme handler:
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #xdg-mime query default x-scheme-handler/https
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #xdg-mime query default x-scheme-handler/http
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #If that returns `org.kde.falkon.desktop`, that's your culprit.
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #Why This Happens
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Right-click → "Copy Image" or clicking to preview within Discord = stays in-app
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Clicking "Open in Browser", or certain link/image previews = uses your default
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #browser, not your default image viewer
28dc9275 [claude-sonnet-5] #- This is normal Discord behavior — it doesn't always download-then-open a local file
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #What You Can Do
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Option 1: Accept it (probably intended)*
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #If you're clicking something like "Open in Browser," this behavior is expected — image mime
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #handlers won't apply.
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Option 2: Right-click → Save/Download, then open manually*
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #This avoids the browser entirely.
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Option 3: Switch default browser* (if this is a broader annoyance)
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #xdg-settings set default-web-browser org.kde.falkon.desktop
28dc9276 [claude-sonnet-5] #
