28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #2. Boot Splash Screen (Plymouth)
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #This is the graphical screen shown during boot, before Plasma even starts — replacing the
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #wall of text output.
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #Arch doesn't include this by default; you have to install and configure Plymouth:
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #sudo pacman -S plymouth
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #Then:
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #1. Add `plymouth` to your `mkinitcpio.conf` hooks (before `filesystems`):
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #   HOOKS=(base udev plymouth autodetect modconf block filesystems keyboard fsck)
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #2. Regenerate initramfs:
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #   sudo mkinitcpio -P
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #3. Add kernel parameter `splash` to your bootloader config (e.g., GRUB or systemd-boot)
28dc9e4a [claude-sonnet-5] #4. Choose/install a Plymouth theme:
28dc9e4b [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4b [claude-sonnet-5] #   plymouth-set-default-theme -l
28dc9e4b [claude-sonnet-5] #   sudo plymouth-set-default-theme -R bgrt
28dc9e4b [claude-sonnet-5] #
28dc9e4b [claude-sonnet-5] #
