28ddd318 [claude-sonnet-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.380 519.2KB 13.41s
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #The term "anonymous" in this context refers specifically to the credential state of
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #the request — not anything about hiding identity from the destination server in a broader sense.
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #What It Actually Means
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #When you set:
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #image.crossOrigin = "anonymous";
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #The browser sends the cross-origin request without:
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Cookies
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #- HTTP authentication headers
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #- TLS client certificates
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #So from the server's point of view, it can't tie the request back to a specific logged-in
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #user session — the request arrives "anonymously," credential-wise. That's the literal sense the
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #spec authors meant: not "untraceable," just "no identifying credentials attached."
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #Compare with the other option:
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #image.crossOrigin = "use-credentials";
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #This explicitly does send cookies/auth — the opposite of anonymous.
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #Why This Distinction Mattered for the Spec
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #The security model CORS was solving wasn't just "can Origin A fetch a resource from Origin B" — it
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #was also "should Origin A's page be able to read personalized data from Origin B using the
28ddd319 [claude-sonnet-5] #visitor's existing login session at B." Naming the default mode "anonymous" made the
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #credential-stripping behavior explicit and self-documenting in code, rather than requiring a
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #doc-lookup to understand what the default request behavior would be.
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #On the Deeper Etymology
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #I don't have solid documented sourcing on the exact WHATWG/W3C working-group discussion where
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #"anonymous" specifically (versus some alternative term) got chosen and bikeshedded — I'd be
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #guessing if I claimed a specific rationale beyond the semantic one above. If you want, I can try to
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #dig for the actual spec issue/PR history, but I don't want to invent a tidier origin story than
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #what's actually documented.
28ddd31a [claude-sonnet-5] #
