2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gpt-5.6-sol 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.028 15.22KB 6.46s
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #That is acceptable for local development, but `.gitignore` only prevents accidental Git tracking—it
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #does not encrypt or hide the key.
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Recommended precautions:
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Ensure `./apikey` is actually ignored with `git check-ignore ./apikey`.
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Restrict permissions: `chmod 600 ./apikey`.
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Grant Deno only the necessary permission: `--allow-read=./apikey`, plus restricted `--allow-net`
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #for the Bunny endpoint.
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Read it server-side only and trim the trailing newline.
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Do not include it in container images, deployments, logs, errors, or responses.
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Prefer an environment variable or hosting secret manager for production.
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Remember that `./apikey` is relative to the process’s current working directory, not necessarily
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #the source file.
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- If it was ever committed—even briefly—remove it from Git history and rotate the Bunny key. Adding
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #it to `.gitignore` afterward is insufficient.
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Also avoid serving the project directory itself as a static web root, since a server
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #misconfiguration could expose the file.
2905e4d7 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
