290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #Backstory
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- The name originally meant KDE Non-Linear Video Editor.
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Jason Wood started the project around 2002.
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- It later became an official KDE project, maintained by community contributors.
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- It is built with Qt and KDE Frameworks.
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- Most media processing is provided by the MLT multimedia framework, which in turn uses
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #FFmpeg extensively.
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #- It supports Linux, Windows, and macOS, although Linux remains its traditional platform.
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #This layered design explains some of its rough edges: Kdenlive coordinates its own interface and
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #timeline with MLT, FFmpeg, effects, codecs, GPU/display systems, and desktop integration. Bugs can
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #arise at several of those boundaries.
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #
290737d8 [gpt-5.6-sol] #On Arch, you can see the installed package details and licence with:
