29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #On 20
29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #That's now in range, so you've fixed the out-of-bounds uniform read. Index 20 in `RoaPalette` is:
29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #G,O,B,A    // (0.40, 0.94, 0.70) at alpha 0.52
29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #Mint green, half transparent. Its opaque twin is index 9 (`G,O,B,O`), and a muted opaque green is
29852c71 [deepseek-flash] #index 4 (`G,B,G,O`). If transparent is what you want, 20 is fine.
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #The dominant cause of darkness is still there
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #`worker_baker.js` `postFlora` still writes zero normals:
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #v.push([mx,my,mz,c, 0,0,0,0]);
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #//                 ^^^^^^^^^ nx,ny,nz
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #And nothing downstream computes them. `TopoTile.onFlora` just stores the surface:
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #onFlora(verts,indices){
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #	this.floraSurface=new Surface(verts,indices,[]);
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #}
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #`addTileShape` calls `addSurface`, not `addFlatSurface`, so it skips the `flatifyVerts →
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #calcNormals` path that `addFlatShape` takes. Result: the tile shader's `dot(normal, sun)` is zero
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #for every flora vertex, so the flora sits at ambient only. Palette index 20's alpha won't save it —
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #it'll still read as a dark mint silhouette.
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #The one-line fix, either side:
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #// wire_topo.js onFlora
29852c72 [deepseek-flash] #onFlora(verts,indices){
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #	this.floraSurface=new Surface(verts,indices,[]);
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #	const zfactor=4.6/(this.level*8.0);
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #	this.floraSurface.calcNormals(zfactor);
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #}
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #Same `zfactor` expression as `onBump`, so shading matches the terrain underneath. Do this first —
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #then you'll actually be judging the palette rather than the missing normals.
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #The worker dig hasn't been started
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #For reference, the current state of the three touchpoints:
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #- `worker_baker.js` `onmessage` — no `dig` case.
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #- `worker_baker.js` `createTopo` — `postFlora(256,8,FloraPen,22)` runs immediately, before any
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #outlines could arrive.
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #- `wire_graphics.js` `buildTile` — `build_roof2` is still `false`, so `digOutline` never runs
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #anywhere either.
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #- `wire_grid.js` — `BasementDepth` is still `4`.
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #So right now neither the main-thread nor the worker dig is active; flora is generated from an undug
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #heightmap regardless.
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #If you want me to write the worker-side patch — `importScripts` of `wire_util.js`, a `dig` command,
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #the `digReady` gate in `refresh()`, and `digOutline` hoisted off `TopoTile` into a free function —
29852c73 [deepseek-flash] #say the word and I'll lay it out as a diff against these files. Otherwise, the `onFlora` normals
