29859a6e [deepseek-flash] #
29859a6e [deepseek-flash] #Without this, `activeTiles` in the report is meaningless. For the orphan set, the smallest safe
29859a6e [deepseek-flash] #change is to stamp `tile.frame=this.frameCount` in `tileGet` so newly created tiles fall inside the
29859a6e [deepseek-flash] #sweep window and are retired if nothing touches them — but check the fetch path first, since a slow
29859a6e [deepseek-flash] #tile could then be swept while loading and re-created next frame.
29859a6e [deepseek-flash] #
29859a6e [deepseek-flash] #Caveats on the numbers
29859a6e [deepseek-flash] #
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #- `orphan` is `cached` minus tiles that have at least been fetched, so it counts both failed loads
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #and `pick`-created tiles. If it climbs steadily, that's the `tileGet` leak.
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #- `surfaceBytes` uses `tris.length * (vertCount>65535?4:2)` — a close match to the GL index buffer,
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #not the JS array's actual footprint.
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #- `layerBytes` counts only what the `Shape` objects retain. Textures are counted globally in
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #`textures`, so a shape's texture cost isn't double-counted but also isn't attributed to its layer.
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #- `topoTiles` levels with no tiles report zero, so an empty level is silent rather than absent —
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #worth showing, since it tells you the grid exists but hasn't fetched.
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #Want this folded into the design doc as a section, or submitted as a patch against the three files?
29859a6f [deepseek-flash] #
