2986fbda [roha]    A substantial codebase — thanks for sharing. A few observations, grouped by what stands out
2986fbda [roha]    and what looks risky. ## Architecture notes The tile system (`TopoGrid` / `TopoTile` /
2986fbda [roha]    `TopoSource`) is cleanly layered: source→tile→baker worker→bumpmap→surface. The `Bumpmap`
2986fbda [roha]    topo/diff/ground triple with `pickElevation`/`pickHeight`/`pickGround` separation is a nice
2986fbda [roha]    way to keep elevation and detail separate — it lets the surface crack logic
2986fbda [roha]    (`CreateTopoSurface`) keep detail verts only where `ground==0 && maxz-minz>12`. `Bits` is a
2986fbda [roha]    tidy little polygon rasterizer using 4×4 packed cells; the `digTopo` / `cropTopo` variants
2986fbda [roha]    read well. The `Shape` instancing layout (16 shorts per instance: 4 floats xyzw + 9 rotated
2986fbda [roha]    matrix as shorts + 3 dim) packed into a single `Int16Array` is efficient, but I'd worry about
2986fbdb [roha]    the `flat` attribute stride computation in `bindAttributes` — it walks `attributes` twice and
2986fbdb [roha]    relies on `flat`-prefixed names appearing after non-flat ones in the same object. If insertion
2986fbdb [roha]    order ever changes that will silently corrupt the VAO. The `Arpeggiator` progression table
2986fbdb [roha]    with mythology names is charming and the state-machine in `Beat()` is compact. ## Things that
2986fbdb [roha]    look like real bugs - `Pixelmap` constructor never writes to `this.rgb` — the loop reads
2986fbdb [roha]    `bytes` and advances `p`, but `rgb` is populated nowhere. The class is effectively a no-op. -
2986fbdb [roha]    `wire_topo.js` `TopoTile.cropOutline` calls `outlinePoints(outline)` but the method defined is
2986fbdb [roha]    `outlinePoints()` with no parameters and it returns `Bits` — signature mismatch. -
2986fbdb [roha]    `TopoTile.drawOutline` references `this.resolution` and `this.pickHeight(...)`, neither of
2986fbdb [roha]    which exist on `TopoTile` (they live on `heightmap`). - `wire_topo.js` `fetchDrawing2` uses
2986fbdb [roha]    undefined `data` and `this.grid`. - `wire_util.js` `EventServer.addEvent`
