2986fbdb [roha]    The `digTopo` path exists but is disabled at two points, and there's an ordering problem
2986fbdb [roha]    you'll hit once you turn it on. Here's the full chain. ## 1. The feature switches In
2986fbdb [roha]    `wire_graphics.js`, `Builder.buildTile` starts with a block of `const` flags. `digOutline` is
2986fbdb [roha]    called from inside the `build_roof2` block: ```js const build_roof=false; const
2986fbdb [roha]    build_roof2=false; // <-- gate on the whole roof block const build_roof_basement=true; // <--
2986fbdb [roha]    gate on digOutline inside it ``` Flip `build_roof2` to `true`. `build_roof_basement` is
2986fbdb [roha]    already `true`, so that's the only flag you need. `build_roof` and
2986fbdb [roha]    `build_roof_geom`/`build_walls_geom` control separate features (scratch drawing, wall
2986fbdb [roha]    geometry) — leave them off initially. ## 2. The ordering problem `meshTile` in
2986fbdb [roha]    `wire_graphics.js` does this, in order: ```js tile.createScratch(AppPlatform.ScratchRes);
