2986fbe1 [roha]    Two separate problems combine here, and the primary one is not in the palette. ## Primary
2986fbe1 [roha]    cause: flora has zero normals The flora surface is posted by `worker_baker.js` with normals
2986fbe1 [roha]    explicitly zeroed: ```js v.push([mx,my,mz,c, 0,0,0,0]); // ^^^^^^^^^ nx,ny,nz all zero ```
2986fbe1 [roha]    Compare with `CreateTopoSurface` in the same worker — also zero normals, but it gets fixed up
2986fbe1 [roha]    afterwards in `TopoTile.onBump`: ```js const surface=CreateTopoSurface(128,16,GroundPen,bump);
2986fbe1 [roha]    const zfactor=4.6/(this.level*8.0); surface.calcNormals(zfactor); // <-- fixes the tile
2986fbe1 [roha]    surface this.topoSurface=surface; ``` Flora has no equivalent. `onFlora` just stores it: ```js
2986fbe1 [roha]    onFlora(verts,indices){ this.floraSurface=new Surface(verts,indices,[]); } ``` And
2986fbe1 [roha]    `addTileShape` does not compute normals the way `addFlatShape` does: ```js
2986fbe1 [roha]    addFlatShape(surface,origin,count){ shape.addFlatSurface(surface); // -> flatifyVerts ->
2986fbe1 [roha]    calcNormals ... } addTileShape(surface,basemap,scratch,origin){ ... shape.addSurface(surface);
2986fbe1 [roha]    // raw verts32, no normal pass ... } ``` The tile shader has `sun` as a uniform and `normal`
2986fbe1 [roha]    as an attribute, so lighting is `dot(normal, sun)`. With normals all zero, that's zero — you
2986fbe1 [roha]    get ambient only, which reads as a very dark flat surface. That's the symptom. Fix: compute
2986fbe1 [roha]    normals for the flora surface, using the same `zfactor` expression as `onBump` so shading is
2986fbe1 [roha]    consistent with the terrain underneath. ```js onFlora(verts,indices){ this.floraSurface=new
2986fbe1 [roha]    Surface(verts,indices,[]); const zfactor=4.6/(this.level*8.0);
2986fbe1 [roha]    this.floraSurface.calcNormals(zfactor); } ``` If you'd rather keep the main thread free, call
2986fbe1 [roha]    `calcNormals` in the worker's `postFlora` before posting — but `calcNormals` uses the
2986fbe1 [roha]    `Surface` class, and `worker_baker.js` doesn't import `wire_surface.js`, so you'd have to
