2986fbe2 [roha]    31 is still out of range — `RoaPalette` in `wire_core.js` has 30 entries, indices 0–29.
2986fbe2 [roha]    Whatever colour you're seeing is coming from the driver's undefined-behaviour read of the
2986fbe2 [roha]    `palette` uniform, which is why it's not what you'd expect. ## How the colour actually gets
2986fbe2 [roha]    picked The vertex `xyzc` attribute carries a colour byte in `c`. In `worker_baker.js`,
2986fbe2 [roha]    `postFlora` writes that byte from the `c` argument, which is `FloraPen`. The tile fragment
2986fbe2 [roha]    shader uses it to index a `palette` uniform: ```js this.RawPalette=new
2986fbe2 [roha]    Float32Array(RoaPalette) // wire_core.js layer.setFloats("palette",gpu.RawPalette); //
2986fbe2 [roha]    wire_graphics.js ``` Each palette entry is 4 floats (r,g,b,a). So both the colour *and* the
2986fbe2 [roha]    transparency come from the same index — the 4th float is alpha. ## The green entries, with
2986fbe2 [roha]    their alpha Reading `RoaPalette`, the entries that read as green are: ```
2986fbe2 [roha]    ╭─────────┬──────────────────────┬─────────┬────────────────────────────────╮ │ Index │ RGB │
2986fbe2 [roha]    Alpha │ Look │ ├─────────┼──────────────────────┼─────────┼────────────────────────────────┤ │
2986fbe2 [roha]    4 │ (0.40, 0.70, 0.40) │ 0.94 │ muted green, **opaque** │ │ 9 │ (0.40, 0.94, 0.70) │ 0.94 │
2986fbe2 [roha]    mint, **opaque** │ │ 15 │ (0.40, 0.70, 0.40) │ 0.52 │ muted green, **transparent** │ │ 20 │
2986fbe2 [roha]    (0.40, 0.94, 0.70) │ 0.52 │ mint, **transparent** │ │ 24 │ (0, 0.40, 0) │ 0.52 │ dark green,
2986fbe2 [roha]    **transparent** │ │ 25 │ (0, 0.40, 0.70) │ 0.52 │ teal, **transparent** │
2986fbe2 [roha]    ╰─────────┴──────────────────────┴─────────┴────────────────────────────────╯ ``` The `O`
2986fbe2 [roha]    constant is `0.94` (opaque-ish), the `A` constant is `0.52` (transparent). So the transparent
2986fbe2 [roha]    green you're seeing is one of the `A`-alpha entries — most likely 15 or 24. If you want an
2986fbe2 [roha]    opaque green, set `FloraPen` to `4` or `9`. ## If none of those is the green you want Add a
