2986fbe2 [roha]    needed are all present, but they're not wired together. ## Why buildings currently show up in
2986fbe2 [roha]    flora Flora is generated in the worker, from the merged heightmap, before any drawing data
2986fbe3 [roha]    reaches the tile: ```js // worker_baker.js createTopo()
2986fbe3 [roha]    heightmap.postFlora(256,8,FloraPen,22); // <-- flora built here heightmap.post(); ``` The mask
2986fbe3 [roha]    inside `postFlora` is purely `diff`-based: ```js const m=this.pickHeightMinMax(x*p,y*p);
2986fbe3 [roha]    if(m.min>floraMin){ // floraMin = 22 const h1=m.max; a[y][x]=h0+h1; } ``` `pickHeight` reads
2986fbe3 [roha]    `this.diff`, and on LiDAR that second channel is high around building edges, so those cells
2986fbe3 [roha]    pass the `>22` test. There is no reference to roofs, ground, or any exclusion mask anywhere in
2986fbe3 [roha]    the worker. ## What already exists that does the right thing `TopoTile.digOutline` (in
2986fbe3 [roha]    `wire_topo.js`) is invoked per roof outline when `build_roof2` is on. It calls `Bits.digTopo`,
2986fbe3 [roha]    which does exactly the zeroing you'd want: ```js // wire_util.js heightmap.setGround(tx+bx,
2986fbe3 [roha]    ty+by, depth); heightmap.setHeight(tx+bx, ty+by, 0); // <-- diff becomes 0 ``` `setHeight`
2986fbe3 [roha]    writes to `diff`, so any cell inside the footprint (plus a `border` halo) fails the `m.min >
2986fbe3 [roha]    floraMin` test. If `TopoFloraSurface` ran *after* `digTopo`, buildings would already be
2986fbe3 [roha]    excluded — no new exclusion logic needed. And `TopoFloraSurface` does exist, in
2986fbe3 [roha]    `wire_core.js`, marked "moved to baker" but never deleted: ```js // moved to baker function
2986fbe3 [roha]    TopoFloraSurface(count,mag,c,topo,floraMin){ ... } ``` It is byte-for-byte the same algorithm
2986fbe3 [roha]    as the worker's `postFlora`, minus the `postMessage`/transfer at the end. ## The ordering
2986fbe3 [roha]    problem The worker runs at fetch time. `digOutline` runs at mesh time, much later, and only
