2986fbf0 [roha]    Compared against the versions I used for the doc, two files changed. Here's what moved and
2986fbf0 [roha]    what it means for the sprint. ## `worker_baker.js` The active flora call changed and
2986fbf0 [roha]    `FloraPen` is now dead: ```js const FloraPen=20; // retained, but no longer referenced ... //
2986fbf0 [roha]    heightmap.postFlora(256,8,FloraPen,22); heightmap.postFlora(512,4,15,2); ``` Three effects: -
2986fbf0 [roha]    **The doc's snippets in §3 and §9 are stale.** They quote `postFlora(256,8,FloraPen,22)`. The
2986fbf0 [roha]    `createTopo` ordering (dig → flora → post) is unaffected, but the literal call needs updating
2986fbf0 [roha]    so the doc doesn't mislead. - **`floraMin` dropped from 22 to 2.** `digTopo` zeroes `diff`, so
2986fbf0 [roha]    a dug cell yields `m.min = 0`, which still fails `m.min > 2`. Exclusion still works — but the
2986fbf0 [roha]    margin is now razor-thin. At `22` there was slack for a leaky border; at `2` any single
2986fbf0 [roha]    non-zero `diff` sample inside the footprint keeps flora. The `border` halo becomes
2986fbf0 [roha]    load-bearing, not cosmetic. This strengthens §16 open question 2 (separate flora clearance vs
2986fbf0 [roha]    basement carve). - **`count` 256→512 doubles the flora grid.** 513² samples instead of 257².
2986fbf0 [roha]    The worker dig now runs in front of a substantially heavier flora pass, which matters for
2986fbf0 [roha]    §13/§14 — the dig cost is small, but it's serialised ahead of a bigger job on the same worker
2986fbf0 [roha]    thread. Worth measuring before committing the estimate. Colour is now hardcoded `15`
2986fbf0 [roha]    (`G,B,G,A` — muted green, alpha 0.52), so the `FloraPen` prerequisite row in §12 should become
