2986fbf1 [roha]    Yes — there's a distinction, but it's derived rather than stored, and one half of it leaks.
2986fbf1 [roha]    That matters because a stats report built on the leaky half will show a number that only ever
2986fbf1 [roha]    grows. ## What "active" currently means Three separate notions exist, and they aren't the same
2986fbf1 [roha]    set: ```
2986fbf1 [roha]    ╭───────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────
2986fbf1 [roha]    ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮ │ Notion │
2986fbf1 [roha]    Where │ Meaning │
2986fbf1 [roha]    ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────
2986fbf1 [roha]    ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤ │
2986fbf1 [roha]    **Touched** │ `TopoTile.frame` vs `TopoGrid.frameCount` │ Set by `touchTiles` for tiles that
2986fbf1 [roha]    are `fetched && ready`; `sweep` removes them once `frame < frameCount-20` │ │ **Meshed** │
2986fbf1 [roha]    `GraphicsStack._activeTiles` │ Pushed in `meshTile`; never removed │ │ **Cached** │
2986fbf1 [roha]    `TopoGrid._tileGrid` │ Everything in the grid, whether touched or not │
2986fbf1 [roha]    ╰───────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────
2986fbf1 [roha]    ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯ ``` So
2986fbf1 [roha]    "active vs cached" is `tile.frame >= frameCount-20` versus the rest of `_tileGrid`. That's
2986fbf1 [roha]    computable. But two things are broken around it: - **`GraphicsStack.flushTile` never splices
2986fbf1 [roha]    `_activeTiles`.** It removes the meshes from the layers and calls `tile.retire()`, but the
2986fbf1 [roha]    tile stays in the array. That array grows for the lifetime of the session, so
2986fbf1 [roha]    `_activeTiles.length` is a leak counter, not an active count. - **`sweep` skips tiles whose
2986fbf1 [roha]    `frame` was never set.** The guard is `if(tile.frame && tile.frame<minFrame)`, and `undefined`
2986fbf2 [roha]    is falsy, so a tile that was created by `tileGet` but never
