2986fbf4 [roha]    Two caveats on the number: - It counts the decoded RGBA footprint of each `<img>` in
2986fbf4 [roha]    `imageStack`, not the GPU texture. They match for aerial because each tile's src is unique, so
2986fbf4 [roha]    nothing is double-counted — but if two tiles ever shared a src, GPU would hold one copy and
2986fbf4 [roha]    this would count two. - The scratch canvas and wallmap per tile are *not* included and are
2986fbf4 [roha]    larger than you'd expect — `ScratchRes=2048` means 16 MB of canvas per tile, versus ~6 MB of
2986fbf4 [roha]    heightmap. If the tiles figure at 9 MB looks low next to the aerial figure, that's why. Say
