2986fbf4 [roha]    Yes — the baker is the only place it can work. `post()` detaches `topo`/`diff`/`ground`, so
2986fbf4 [roha]    the dig has exactly one window: after the merge, before `postFlora`. That window is inside the
2986fbf4 [roha]    worker. ## Message ```js {command:"dig", outlines, depth, border} ``` `outlines` is the array
2986fbf4 [roha]    of `drawing.outlines[start+i]` vertex arrays. Plain structured clone, no transfer list.
2986fbf4 [roha]    `depth`/`border` sent from main so the knobs stay in `wire_grid.js`. ## Worker state and gate
2986fbf4 [roha]    `refresh()` currently fires on `topoCount==heightmaps.length` alone. It needs a second gate,
2986fbf4 [roha]    because the outlines arrive on a different fetch. ```js let topoCount; let digReady=false; let
2986fbf5 [roha]    digDepth=4; let digBorder=40; const heightmaps=[]; const roofOutlines=[]; function refresh(){
2986fbf5 [roha]    if(topoCount==heightmaps.length && digReady){ createTopo(); } } ``` ```js case "dig":
2986fbf5 [roha]    onDig(line.outlines,line.depth,line.border); break; ``` ```js function
2986fbf5 [roha]    onDig(outlines,depth,border){ for(const outline of outlines){ roofOutlines.push(outline); }
2986fbf5 [roha]    digDepth=depth; digBorder=border; digReady=true; refresh(); } ``` Accumulate rather than
2986fbf5 [roha]    replace, so multiple drawings on one tile merge. ## Ordering in `createTopo` The whole point.
2986fbf5 [roha]    Dig, then flora, then post: ```js function createTopo(){ const bytes=heightmaps[0]||[]; const
2986fbf5 [roha]    heightmap=AllocBumpmap(bytes); heightmap.setBytes(bytes); const n=heightmaps.length; for(let
2986fbf5 [roha]    i=1;i<n;i++){ if(heightmaps[i].length==bytes.length){ heightmap.orBytes(heightmaps[i]); } }
2986fbf5 [roha]    heightmaps.length=0; for(const outline of roofOutlines){
2986fbf5 [roha]    digOutline(heightmap,outline,digDepth,digBorder); } roofOutlines.length=0;
2986fbf5 [roha]    heightmap.postFlora(512,4,15,2); heightmap.post(); } ``` `digOutline` uses only
2986fbf5 [roha]    `heightmap.pickTopo` and `heightmap.setGround/setHeight`, and the worker's own `Bumpmap`
2986fbf5 [roha]    implements all three — so the same free
2986fbf5 [roha]    fun
