299c9c1b [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.025 1.277MB 44.15s
299c9c1b [deepseek-flash] #Read the batch against the previous versions. Several real changes, and two of them mean the dig
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #feature is currently inert. Details below.
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #1. Duplicate `refresh()` — the dig gate is dead
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #`worker_baker.js` now declares `refresh` twice:
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #function refresh(){
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #	if(topoCount==heightmaps.length && digReady){	// first
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #		createTopo();
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #	}
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #}
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #...
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #function refresh(){
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #	if(topoCount==heightmaps.length){				// second, later in file
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #		createTopo();
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #	}
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #}
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #Function declarations hoist and the last one wins. So the live `refresh` is the ungated
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #version: `digReady` is never consulted, `onDig` is never required, and `createTopo` fires on the
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #topo count alone.
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #That's actually why tiles still load. If you delete the second declaration and keep the gated one,
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #tiles will hang forever, because the main thread never sends `dig` (no `maybeSendDig` in
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #`wire_topo.js`). So the duplicate is masking a missing sender. Decide which way you want it:
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1c [deepseek-flash] #- Keep it simple for now: delete the first (gated) declaration, accept no dig, and wire `dig`
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #later.
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #- Or wire the sender and delete the second.
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #Right now `digReady` is a dead variable and `createTopo`'s `digReady=true;` does nothing.
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #2. `digOutline` is undefined in the worker
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #`createTopo` calls it:
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #for(const outline of roofOutlines){
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #	digOutline(heightmap,outline,digDepth,digBorder);
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #}
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #But `worker_baker.js` has no `digOutline`, no `Bits`, and no `importScripts`. It only survives
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #because `roofOutlines` is always empty. The moment a `dig` message lands, that's a `ReferenceError`
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #and the worker dies silently (no `onerror` handler), so the tile never meshes.
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #Also `//	roofOutlines.length=0;` is commented out, so if `createTopo` ever ran twice the same
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #outlines would be re-dug.
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #3. Flora: two generators, and the main one is broken
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #`meshTile` now builds its own flora and ignores the worker's:
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #const floraSurface=TopoFloraSurface(256,8,0,tile.heightmap);
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #const floramesh=layer0.addTileShape(floraSurface,tile.basemap,tile.scratch,origin);
299c9c1d [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #Two problems in that one call:
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #• Missing `floraMin`.* Signature is `TopoFloraSurface(count,mag,c,topo,floraMin)`. You pass
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #four args, so `floraMin` is `undefined`. Inside:
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #if(m.min>floraMin){		// number > undefined → NaN compare → always false
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #So nothing passes the mask, `a[y][x]` is never set, and the surface comes out empty. No flora
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #renders.
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #• `c` is in the wrong slot.* `TopoFloraSurface` writes:
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #v.push([mx,my,mz,15, 0,0,0,c]);
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #//                  ^^ index 3 is the colour, not index 7
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #Index 3 is the palette index; index 7 is the `bits`/w slot (see `CreateTopoSurface`). So the colour
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #is hardcoded `15` — the original transparent green — and your `c=0` lands in the wrong field.
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #That's the "current transparent green" you were trying to change.
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #So there are two flora generators running (worker `FloraPen=3` at count 128, main at count 256) and
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #neither shows. The worker's is wasted work, the main one is empty.
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #• Pick one.* Cleanest is to drop the main-thread generation and use the worker's, which
299c9c1e [deepseek-flash] #already respects `FloraPen`:
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #// wire_graphics.js — meshTile
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #const floraSurface=tile.floraSurface;
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #const floramesh=layer0.addTileShape(floraSurface,tile.basemap,tile.scratch,origin);
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #tile.floramesh=floramesh;
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #If you'd rather keep main-thread flora, fix `TopoFloraSurface` (`15` → `c`, and pass a `floraMin`).
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #4. `ScratchRes` clip mismatch
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #`wire_graphics.js` now has `let ScratchRes=1024;`, and `TraceClosedOutline` uses it as the clip
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #box:
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #const clip=ScratchRes;
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #...
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #if(px>=clip&&x<clip) enterEdge=2;
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #But outline coordinates are `v[0]/2` → range `0..2048`, and the scratch canvas is
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #`AppPlatform.ScratchRes=2048` with `ScratchScale=1.0`. So the traced roof path is clipped to a 1024
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #box on a 2048 canvas — every roof in the right/bottom half is cut off, and the basement fill leaks
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #the wrong shape. Set `ScratchRes=2048` (or feed it from `AppPlatform.ScratchRes`).
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #Smaller things
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c1f [deepseek-flash] #- `auditGrid` mislabels. `count` increments per grid level, not per tile, and is printed as
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #`"[AUDIT] tiles:"+count`. There's no tile count at all. If you want the count, accumulate inside
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #the `x`/`y` loops.
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #- `postFlora` dead loop. The new `if(!e){ let h0=this.pickElevation(...); }` block does
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #nothing (`h0` unused, assignment commented). Looks like a leftover gap-fill experiment.
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #- `roofCount` unused in the `build_roof2` block; `TraceClosedOutline` is now uncommented,
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #so roofs trace into the clip path. That's a real behaviour change — the `#555` fill now covers roof
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #footprints.
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #- `build_roof_basement=false` on main, so `tile.digOutline` no longer runs anywhere
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #(worker's is inert per §1–2). The dig is currently fully off.
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #- `_activeTiles` still never spliced in `flushTile`, so the draw-order note from last turn
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #is unchanged — mesh order is still load order.
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #Suggested order
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #1. Delete the duplicate `refresh` (decide gate vs no-gate).
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #2. Fix flora: use `tile.floraSurface`, or fix `TopoFloraSurface`'s colour slot and `floraMin`.
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #3. `ScratchRes=2048`.
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #4. Only then add `importScripts`/`digOutline` + the main-thread `dig` sender.
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #Want me to write the worker diff (single `refresh`, `importScripts`, guard) and the `meshTile`
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #flora swap?
299c9c20 [deepseek-flash] #
